## 7. Quick Reference Checklist

| # | Rule | Smell to look for |
|---|------|--------------------|
| 1.1 | Small, single-purpose functions | Function name contains "and" |
| 1.2 | Intention-revealing names | `d`, `p`, `flag1`, `temp` |
| 1.3 | No magic numbers/strings | Bare literals in conditionals |
| 1.4 | Guard clauses | 3+ levels of nested `if` |
| 1.5 | DRY | Same logic copy-pasted in 2+ places |
| 1.6 | One level of abstraction | High-level and low-level code interleaved |
| 1.7 | Named parameters | 3+ positional params, especially same-typed |
| 1.8 | Specific exceptions | `throw Exception('error')` |
| 2.1 | Encapsulation | Public mutable fields with invariants |
| 2.2 | Composition over inheritance | Deep `extends` chains for unrelated capabilities |
| 2.3 | Program to interfaces | `final Concrete _dep = Concrete();` |
| 3.1–3.5 | SOLID | See §3 for the specific smell per principle |
| 4.1 | Enhanced enums | `if (role == 'admin')` string comparisons |
| 4.2 | Sealed classes | Nullable/boolean-flag soup modeling state |
| 4.3 | Records | Throwaway class just to return 2–3 values |
| 4.4 | Pattern matching | `is Type` + manual cast chains |
| 4.5 | Extensions | `Utils.doThing(value)` static helper classes |
| 4.6 | Mixins | Shared base class for unrelated hierarchies |
| 5.1 | Explicit optionality | `String?` fields that are never actually null |
| 5.2 | Immutability by default | Mutable fields with no mutation need |
| 5.3 | Null-aware operators | Manual `if (x != null)` before every use |
